{
  "rationale": "The design separates unconstrained sensing/actuation capability in the plant from a deterministic safety-and-coverage policy in the specifications. The policy uses random_walk as the default clear-state exploration action, inserts a short forward pulse after random exploration to bias coverage, and routes every obstacle event through a dedicated turn-recovery state. Front obstacles trigger a conservative directed turn, side obstacles bias turning away from the blocked side, and full_rotate is reserved only for a dedicated last-resort recovery state.",
  "strategy": [
    "Model sensing and motion as separate plant automata so the supervisor can constrain behavior without inventing new events",
    "Use small deterministic specifications: one for clear-state exploration alternation, one for front-obstacle recovery, one for left-obstacle recovery, one for right-obstacle recovery, and one sparse escape specification enabling full_rotate only in a dedicated blocked state"
  ],
